Subject: [PATCH] tests: resolve SONiC dependencies in nested Bazel fixtures

The registry dependency refresh selects Gazelle 0.54.0.sonic.2. The upstream
bazel_testing helper creates a fresh workspace with only BCR configured, so
the retained native build-ID regression tests fail before compiling their
fixtures. Pass the existing helper's GO_BAZEL_TEST_BAZELFLAGS interface the
same immutable SONiC registry catalog used by this dependency refresh, then
BCR for public modules. The helper's local_path_override continues to use
the actual rules_go candidate under test. No assertions, fixture source,
SDK selection, architecture or production code is changed.

This is SONiC registry test configuration, not an upstream production fix.
Remove it when the nested fixture receives the parent registry configuration
through an upstream interface or these module versions are available in BCR.

--- a/tests/core/go_binary/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/tests/core/go_binary/BUILD.bazel
@@ -345,7 +345,12 @@
     name = "sonic_linux_buildid_test",
     srcs = ["buildid_test.go"],
     args = ["-test.v", "-test.run=^(TestContentBuildID|TestNativeChangeChangesBuildID)$$"],
-    env = {"USE_BAZEL_VERSION": "8.5.1"},
+    env = {
+        # The upstream helper writes these flags into its nested .bazelrc.
+        # Its existing local_path_override still selects this candidate.
+        "GO_BAZEL_TEST_BAZELFLAGS": "--registry=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sonic-net/sonic-bazel-registry/f9a9baaeabad4a77c3ad5939fe257434e635e0dc --registry=https://bcr.bazel.build",
+        "USE_BAZEL_VERSION": "8.5.1",
+    },
     target_compatible_with = ["@platforms//os:linux"],
     timeout = "long",
 )
